+The official cards say recent upstream llama.cpp supports the Bonsai **Q2_0** group-64 file and rejects **PTQ1_0/PQ2_0** as unknown types. The exact Serea pin's `ggml/include/ggml.h` contains `GGML_TYPE_Q2_0` but neither `GGML_TYPE_PTQ1_0` nor `GGML_TYPE_PQ2_0`, confirming the latter formats cannot be loaded by that fixed source. Therefore the matrix marks the documented default packings incompatible and keeps any Q2_0 path NOT_RUN; no silent source upgrade is proposed.
+
+The official PrismML fork at `c96baf4abe24d11a50f326e40b6223b687449d63` advertises these packs and its source has private PTQ1_0/PQ2_0 types and CPU quantization dispatch. Its documentation includes Android NDK builds and an Android example; it describes Arm acceleration and contains Arm CPU feature paths. This makes a separate Android adapter experiment plausible, but is not an Android model-load result. The Bonsai cards list CPU/CUDA/Metal, not Vulkan; fork-wide Vulkan availability does not prove Bonsai quant kernels on Vulkan, so Vulkan stays NOT_RUN. Pixel 7a ARM64, ARM NEON behavior under the model kernels, and Android Vulkan remain NOT_RUN.
